<!-- HEADER -->
<div class="report-header">
  <div class="meta">Trend Analysis Report &bull; PubMed Biomedical Research &bull; April 2026</div>
  <h1>Biomedical Research Landscape 2024–2026: Publication Trends, Topic Dynamics, and Open Access Patterns</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">A strategic intelligence briefing based on 126,832 biomedical research abstracts indexed in PubMed from January 2024 through March 2026. Prepared for research policy analysts and funding strategists.</p>
  <div class="header-stats">
    <div class="header-stat"><div class="value">126,832</div><div class="label">Total Abstracts</div></div>
    <div class="header-stat"><div class="value">65.1%</div><div class="label">Open Access Rate</div></div>
    <div class="header-stat"><div class="value">6</div><div class="label">Median Authors</div></div>
    <div class="header-stat"><div class="value">Jan 2024 – Mar 2026</div><div class="label">Coverage Window</div></div>
    <div class="header-stat"><div class="value">150+</div><div class="label">Countries</div></div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- MAIN BODY -->
<div class="main">

  <!-- TABLE OF CONTENTS -->
  <div class="toc">
    <h3>Contents</h3>
    <ol>
      <li><a href="#pub-volume">Publication Volume &amp; Temporal Distribution</a></li>
      <li><a href="#geo">Geographic Landscape of Biomedical Research</a></li>
      <li><a href="#topics">Research Topic &amp; MeSH Keyword Analysis</a></li>
      <li><a href="#oa">Open Access Adoption &amp; Journal Landscape</a></li>
      <li><a href="#types">Research Type Distribution &amp; Collaboration Indicators</a></li>
      <li><a href="#takeaways">Key Takeaways &amp; Strategic Implications</a></li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <!-- KPI STRIP -->
  <div class="kpi-grid">
    <div class="kpi-card">
      <div class="kpi-value">126,832</div>
      <div class="kpi-label">Total Publications</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">2024–Mar 2026 window</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card accent2">
      <div class="kpi-value">65.1%</div>
      <div class="kpi-label">Open Access Rate</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">Rising: 64.1% → 74.1%</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card accent3">
      <div class="kpi-value">6</div>
      <div class="kpi-label">Median Authors</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">Mean: 7.1 per article</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card accent4">
      <div class="kpi-value">52.4%</div>
      <div class="kpi-label">Top 10 Countries Share</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">China leads at 22.1%</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card accent5">
      <div class="kpi-value">1,659</div>
      <div class="kpi-label">Unique MeSH Topics</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">COVID-19 most frequent</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- SECTION 1: Publication Volume -->
  <div class="section" id="pub-volume">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-num">1</div>
      <div>
        <div class="section-title">Publication Volume &amp; Temporal Distribution</div>
        <div class="section-desc">Monthly and yearly publication counts; PubMed indexing lag context</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="insight warning">
      <strong>Indexing Lag Advisory:</strong> Approximately 80% of records (est. ~101,860) originate from 2024. This is an expected real-world artifact of PubMed's indexing pipeline — articles accumulate more indexed entries over time. 2025 (~19,131) and 2026 (~5,841 through March only) figures underrepresent actual output. All cross-year comparisons use normalized rates, not raw counts.
    </div>

    <div class="chart-grid chart-grid-2" style="margin-top:20px;">
      <div class="chart-card">
        <h3>Estimated Annual Publication Volume</h3>
        <p>Projected from 4,886-record analytical sample scaled to full dataset (126,832 abstracts)</p>
        <div class="chart-container" style="height:260px;">
          <canvas id="yearlyVolumeChart"></canvas>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="chart-card">
        <h3>Monthly Publication Volume — 2024 (Known Months)</h3>
        <p>Records with identified publication months; "Unknown" month records excluded from trend line</p>
        <div class="chart-container" style="height:260px;">
          <canvas id="monthly2024Chart"></canvas>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="chart-card" style="margin-top:20px;">
      <h3>Monthly Volume Trend — All Years (Known Months Only)</h3>
      <p>Temporal publication flow across the 2024–2026 window; early 2024 spike reflects indexing of pre-2024 backlog ingested at dataset creation</p>
      <div class="chart-container" style="height:280px;">
        <canvas id="allMonthlyChart"></canvas>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="insight">
      <strong>Key Pattern:</strong> January 2024 shows an anomalous peak of ~43,215 estimated publications — significantly above subsequent months (~7,800–10,000 range). This spike almost certainly reflects bulk PubMed indexing of prior-year articles at the start of the data collection window, not a real publication surge. Analysts should treat Jan-2024 as a structural artifact when modeling growth rates.
    </div>

    <div class="caveat">Note: Monthly figures are derived from records with identified pub_month values. 575 records (11.8% of 2024 sample) and 179 records (24.3% of 2025 sample) have unknown publication months and are excluded from monthly trends but included in annual totals.</div>
  </div>

  <!-- SECTION 2: Geographic -->
  <div class="section" id="geo">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-num">2</div>
      <div>
        <div class="section-title">Geographic Landscape of Biomedical Research</div>
        <div class="section-desc">Top contributing countries, geographic concentration, and open-access rates by nation</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="chart-grid chart-grid-2">
      <div class="chart-card">
        <h3>Top 12 Countries by Publication Volume</h3>
        <p>China and USA accounts for flagged values; "PR China" and "People's Republic of China" unified with "China"</p>
        <div class="chart-container" style="height:320px;">
          <canvas id="countryBarChart"></canvas>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="chart-card">
        <h3>Geographic Concentration</h3>
        <p>Share of total publications by top-country groups</p>
        <div class="chart-container" style="height:320px;">
          <canvas id="geoShareChart"></canvas>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-top:20px;" class="chart-card">
      <h3>Country-Level Open Access Rate (Top 10 Countries)</h3>
      <p>Proportion of OA publications per country; Iran leads at 86.9%, China is lowest major producer at 55.5%</p>
      <div class="chart-container" style="height:260px;">
        <canvas id="countryOAChart"></canvas>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-top:20px;" class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>#</th>
            <th>Country</th>
            <th class="num">Publications (Sample)</th>
            <th class="num">Est. Full Dataset</th>
            <th class="num">Share %</th>
            <th class="num">OA Rate %</th>
            <th class="num">Median Authors</th>
            <th class="bar-cell">Volume</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
